## Find three pairs of equal sides
Compare triangle $ABD$ with triangle $ACD$.
|AB| &= |AC| \qquad \text{(given: triangle } ABC \text{ is isosceles)}
|BD| &= |DC| \qquad \text{(} D \text{ is the midpoint of } [BC] \text{)}
|AD| &= |AD| \qquad \text{(common side)}
## State the conclusion
All three sides of one triangle equal the three sides of the other.
\triangle ABD &\equiv \triangle ACD \qquad \text{(SSS)}
ANSWER: \triangle ABD \equiv \triangle ACD \text{ (SSS)}

## Write the volume formula equal to 5424.6
\frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 &= 5424.6
## Isolate r cubed
4\pi r^3 &= 3 \times 5424.6
4\pi r^3 &= 16273.8
r^3 &= \frac{16273.8}{4\pi}
r^3 &= 1295.027\ldots
## Take the cube root and round to 1 decimal place
r &= \sqrt[3]{1295.027\ldots}
&= 10.899\ldots
&\approx 10.9 \text{ cm}
ANSWER: 10.9 \text{ cm}

## Divide the bigger side by the smaller side
The scale factor is the length on the bigger table-top divided by the length on the smaller one.
k &= \frac{45}{36}
k &= 1.25
## Multiply the shortest side by the scale factor
\text{Length} &= 25.5 \times 1.25
