## Add up the six sides
There are four sides of 200 m and two sides of 150 m.
\text{Total} &= 4 \times 200 + 2 \times 150
&= 800 + 300
&= 1100 \text{ m}
ANSWER: 1100 \text{ m}

## Isolate the term containing p
\frac{1}{n} + \frac{2}{p} &= \frac{3}{s}
\frac{2}{p} &= \frac{3}{s} - \frac{1}{n}
## Combine the right-hand side over a common denominator
The common denominator of $s$ and $n$ is $sn$.
\frac{2}{p} &= \frac{3n}{sn} - \frac{s}{sn}
\frac{2}{p} &= \frac{3n - s}{sn}
## Turn both sides upside down
\frac{p}{2} &= \frac{sn}{3n - s}
## Multiply both sides by 2
p &= 2 \times \frac{sn}{3n - s}
p &= \frac{2sn}{3n - s}
ANSWER: p = \frac{2sn}{3n - s}

## Write the number as 4 plus an infinite series
Each repeat of 36 is 100 times smaller than the one before.
4.363636\ldots &= 4 + \frac{36}{100} + \frac{36}{100^2} + \frac{36}{100^3} + \cdots
## Identify the geometric series
After the 4, the series is geometric.
a &= \frac{36}{100}
r &= \frac{1}{100}
## Substitute into the sum to infinity formula
S_\infty &= \frac{a}{1 - r}
S_\infty &= \frac{\frac{36}{100}}{1 - \frac{1}{100}}
S_\infty &= \frac{\frac{36}{100}}{\frac{99}{100}}
S_\infty &= \frac{36}{99}
## Add the whole number 4
4 + \frac{36}{99} &= \frac{396}{99} + \frac{36}{99}
&= \frac{432}{99}
## Simplify by dividing top and bottom by 9
\frac{432}{99} &= \frac{48}{11}
ANSWER: 4.\dot{3}\dot{6} = \frac{48}{11}
